    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7303" root="حدب" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَدِبٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَحْدَبُ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also (tropical:)  <i>Affectionate, favourable,</i> or <i>kind.</i> (A, TA.) You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُوَ حَدِبٌ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَلَى أَخِيهِ</span> (tropical:)  <i>He is affectionate,</i> &amp;c., <i>to his brother.</i>
(A.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْضٌ حَدِبَةٌ</span> <i>A land abounding with the
plant called</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَدَب</span>. (K.)

